interesting sites","icon":"","description":"\n<a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"external-link is-unresolved\" href=\"https://github.com/Save2541/1DEMPyPIC\" target=\"_self\">https://github.com/Save2541/1DEMPyPIC</a>\n<br><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"external-link is-unresolved\" href=\"https://github.com/GangMei-CUGB/juSPH\" target=\"_self\">https://github.com/GangMei-CUGB/juSPH</a>\n<br><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"external-link is-unresolved\" href=\"https://github.com/ElsevierSoftwareX/SOFTX-D-22-00107\" target=\"_self\">https://github.com/ElsevierSoftwareX/SOFTX-D-22-00107</a>\n<br><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"external-link is-unresolved\" href=\"https://github.com/SebastianM-C/PICDataStructures.jl\" target=\"_self\">https://github.com/SebastianM-C/PICDataStructures.jl</a>\n","aliases":[],"inlineTags":[],"frontmatterTags":[],"headers":[],"links":[],"author":"","coverImageURL":"","fullURL":"links-to-interesting-sites.html","pathToRoot":".","attachments":[],"createdTime":1783948796517,"modifiedTime":1783965618875,"sourceSize":251,"sourcePath":"4_Project/Physics PhD/Links to interesting sites.md","exportPath":"links-to-interesting-sites.html","showInTree":true,"treeOrder":2,"backlinks":[],"type":"markdown"},"literature-review.html":{"title":"Literature Review","icon":"","description":"\nComputational Plasma Science - Physics &amp; Selected Simulation Examples (Shigeo Kawata) A preliminary investigation of the pseudo-spectral method numerical solution of the Perkins instability equations in the homogeneous TEC case (Q. Zhou, J. Mathews, Q. Du, C. Miller) - 2004\nCoupling of the Perkins instability and the sporadic E layer instability derived from physical arguments (R. Cosgrove, R. Tsunoda, S. Fukao, M. Yamamoto) - 2004\nFirst three-dimensional simulation of the Perkins instability in the nighttime midlatitude ionosphere (T. Yokoyama, Y. Otsuka, T. Ogawa, M. Yamamoto, D. Hysell) - 2008\nNumerical simulation of Perkins instability in the midlatitude F-region ionosphere: The influence of background ionospheric multi-factors (Y. Liu, T. Lam, Y. Zhou, Y. Zhu, Z. Fan, Y. Wu, Y. Zhang, X. Wang) - 2025\nOn the physical explanation of the Perkins instability (Q. Zhou, J. Mathews) - 2006\nParametric instabilities and ionospheric modification (F. Perkins, C. Oberman, E. Valeo) - 1974\nPerkins instability revisited (A. Hamza) - 1999\nThe evolution of nighttime mid-latitude mesoscale F-region structures: A case study utilizing numerical solution of the Perkins instability equations (Q. Zhou, J. Mathews, C. Miller, I. Seker) - 2006\nThree-dimensional simulation of the coupled Perkins and -layer instabilities in the nighttime midlatitude ionosphere (T. Yokoyama, D. Hysell, Y. Otsuka, M. Yamamoto) - 2009 Fundamentals of numerical modeling of the mid-latitude ionosphere (G. Jee) - 2023\nThe evolution of nighttime mid-latitude mesoscale F-region structures: A case study utilizing numerical solution of the Perkins instability equations (Q. Zhou, J. Mathews, C. Miller, I. Seker) - 2006 eduPIC: An introductory particle based code for radio-frequency plasma simulation (Z. Donko, A. Derzsi, M. Vass, B. Horvath, S. Wilczek, B. Hartmann, P. Hartmann) - 2021\nHigher-order particle representation for particle-in-cell simulations (D. Brown, M. Bettencourt, S. Wright, S. Maheswaran, J. Jones, S. Jarvis) - 2021\nMHD-PIC connection model of auroral arc formation process in a magnetosphere-ionosphere coupling system (T. Sugiyama, K. Kusano, S. Hirose, A. Kageyama, K. Watanabe, T. Sato) Orb5: A global electromagnetic gyrokinetic code using the PIC approach in toroidal geometry (E. Lanti, et al) - 2020\nParticle-in-cell codes for plasma-based particle acceleration (A. Pukhov) - 2016\nParticle-in-cell simulation using asynchronous tasking (N. Guidotti, P. Ceyrat, J. Barreto, J. Monteiro, R. Rodrigues, R. Fonseca, X. Martonell, A. Pena) - 2021\nStep-by-step verification of particle-in-cell Monte Carlo collision codes (P. Parodi, F. Petronio) - 2025\nStructure and dynamics of a new class of thin current sheets (M. Sitnov, M. Swisdak, P. Guzdar, A. Runov) - 2006\nUnified fluid-model theory of ExB instabilities in low-ionized collisional plasmas with arbitrarily magnetized multi-species ions (Y. Dimant, M. Oppenheim, S. Evans, J. Martinez-Sykora) - 2023\n","aliases":[],"inlineTags":[],"frontmatterTags":[],"headers":[{"heading":"Textbooks","level":2,"id":"Textbooks_0"},{"heading":"Perkins Instability","level":2,"id":"Perkins_Instability_0"},{"heading":"Mid-latitude Physics/Simulations","level":2,"id":"Mid-latitude_Physics/Simulations_0"},{"heading":"PIC Codes/Simulations","level":2,"id":"PIC_Codes/Simulations_0"}],"links":[],"author":"","coverImageURL":"","fullURL":"literature-review.html","pathToRoot":".","attachments":[],"createdTime":1793032474860,"modifiedTime":1793925972705,"sourceSize":3174,"sourcePath":"4_Project/Physics PhD/Literature Review.md","exportPath":"literature-review.html","showInTree":true,"treeOrder":3,"backlinks":["physics-phd.html"],"type":"markdown"},"physics-phd.html":{"title":"Physics PhD","icon":"","description":"I have started the process for my PhD in Physics. This project note will act as a MOC for the process.\nThe literature review is tracked at <a data-href=\"4_Project/Physics PhD/Literature Review\" href=\"literature-review.html\" class=\"internal-link\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">4_Project/Physics PhD/Literature Review</a> fill out the grad update 📅 2023-11-16\nfill out grad update 📅 2024-11-13 ✅ 2024-12-02\nFill out SGS annual progress report 📅 2026-12-01\nFill out Program of study form 2026-11-01 22:05 - finding articles of numerical simulations of mid-latitude ionospheric systems\n2024-05-21 - Updates finished quantum class - A-\nfinished E&amp;M class - B-\nverified with Abdulhaq that I am good to continue 2023-08-22 - Courses have been registered for, and the tuition waiver has been sent in.\n2023-08-16 - Catch up note. Dr. Hamza said that he will reach out to Jay and William to be on my supervisory committee.\n","aliases":[],"inlineTags":[],"frontmatterTags":["#Projects/PhD","#favorite"],"headers":[{"heading":"Steps of study","level":1,"id":"Steps_of_study_0"},{"heading":"Literature Review","level":2,"id":"Literature_Review_0"},{"heading":"Code development","level":2,"id":"Code_development_0"},{"heading":"Comparison with recent simulations","level":2,"id":"Comparison_with_recent_simulations_0"},{"heading":"Comparison with experimental measurements","level":2,"id":"Comparison_with_experimental_measurements_0"},{"heading":"Todos","level":2,"id":"Todos_0"},{"heading":"Log","level":2,"id":"Log_0"}],"links":["literature-review.html"],"author":"","coverImageURL":"","fullURL":"physics-phd.html","pathToRoot":".","attachments":[],"createdTime":1692235477708,"modifiedTime":1793632823311,"sourceSize":1108,"sourcePath":"4_Project/Physics PhD/Physics PhD.md","exportPath":"physics-phd.html","showInTree":true,"treeOrder":4,"backlinks":[],"type":"markdown"}},"fileInfo":{"progress-reports/test.html":{"createdTime":1793927135835,"modifiedTime":1793927527264,"sourceSize":74,"sourcePath":"4_Project/Physics PhD/Progress Reports/test.md","exportPath":"progress-reports/test.html","showInTree":true,"treeOrder":1,"backlinks":[],"type":"markdown","data":null},"links-to-interesting-sites.html":{"createdTime":1783948796517,"modifiedTime":1783965618875,"sourceSize":251,"sourcePath":"4_Project/Physics PhD/Links to interesting sites.md","exportPath":"links-to-interesting-sites.html","showInTree":true,"treeOrder":2,"backlinks":[],"type":"markdown","data":null},"literature-review.html":{"createdTime":1793032474860,"modifiedTime":1793925972705,"sourceSize":3174,"sourcePath":"4_Project/Physics PhD/Literature Review.md","exportPath":"literature-review.html","showInTree":true,"treeOrder":3,"backlinks":["physics-phd.html"],"type":"markdown","data":null},"physics-phd.html":{"createdTime":1692235477708,"modifiedTime":1793632823311,"sourceSize":